At the `applyPattern` call site, that means the outer `while` loop sees the same quote again and again, repeatedly appending to the buffer until memory is exhausted. That matches the observed `OutOfMemoryError`.

The patch changes that behavior by advancing `pos`:

```java
if (escapingOn && c[start] == QUOTE) {
    pos.setIndex(pos.getIndex() + 1);
}
```

So the parser no longer gets stuck on the same character, which removes the infinite-growth/OOM mechanism.

